AU  - DUNN, TB
TI  - ATTEMPT TO DETECT A MAMMARY TUMOR-AGENT IN STRAIN-C MICE BY X-RADIATION
T2  - JNCI-JOURNAL OF THE NATIONAL CANCER INSTITUTE
AB  - Hybrid mice derived from low-mammary-tumor-strain females and high-mammary-tumor-strain males show a low incidence of mammary tumors because they do not obtain the mammary tumor agent in their mother''s milk. An exception to this rule was noted in hybrids obtained from strain C females and strain C3H males, for such hybrids, if permitted to bear 3 or more litters, show an incidence of at least 50% mammary tumors at an avg. age of 20 mos. or more. On the assumption that strain C females harbored a weak or masked tumor agent, they were exposed to whole-body X-ray radiation to enhance the activity of the agent. To determine whether irradiation had affected the agent, the strain C females were bred to strain C3H males and their offspring observed for the occurrence of mammary tumors. X-irradiation did not reveal the presence of the agent in strain C females. The results confirmed the occurrence of tumors in older agent-free hybrids born to C females and C3H males, as well as the occurrence of tumors in a few young hybrids that contained the agent. There was a random distr. of hybrids containing the agent and available evidence indicated that they had acquired their father''s agent in utero. Furthermore, there was evidence that, on occasion, the infected embryos had infected their strain C mothers. Thus, the mammary tumor agent from C3H male mice may be transmitted to C x C3H offspring and to the strain C females to which they are bred. Histological studies of the tumors arising in older hybrids showed that they fell into 4 groups. 3 groups were adeno-carcinomas. In the 1st group, the acinar structure predominated. The 2d group showed little acinar formation but possessed a variable pattern of solid groups of epithelial cells, single layers of cuboidal cells lining cystic spaces or growing as papillary projections into cysts, and cords of cells separated by a heavy stroma. The 3d group contained many small cysts and epithelial proliferation in the interstitial tissue. The 4th group of tumors were adenoacanthomas showing large areas of squamous-cell elements.
