AU  - FARAVELLI, M
TI  - ONE-DAY CLOTRIMAZOLE (CANESTEN) TREATMENT IN CANDIDAL VULVOVAGINITIS
T2  - CLINICAL TRIALS JOURNAL
AB  - The results are reported of a comparative, completely randomized trial in which 2 groups of 29 female patients suffering from candidal vulvovaginitis were given a single clotrimazole 500 mg pessary or 1 econazole 150 mg pessary for 3 consecutive days. Overall success rates were 92.7% in the clotrimazole group and 32.5% in the econazole group 1 mo. after treatment. Microbiological findings were negative in 92.7% of patients in the clotrimazole group and in 12.5% of patients in the econazole group. No side effects were noted in either group. The tolerance of both drugs was good. The results obtained with clotrimazole compare favorably with the 93% cure rate reported by the 6-day and with the 89.4% overall success rate by the 3-day course of clotrimazole. One day courses of clotrimazole treatment are effective and well tolerated and are valuable in dealing with uncooperative women who stop treatment at the earliest possible moment. It is recommended that a repeat single-dose treatment be given to patients with a history of candidiasis, ideally 3 to 5 wk after the first dose; that in every patient an antimicotic cream should be applied to the vulvo-perineal area and that partners should also be treated; and that in such patients a thorough search should be made for probable precipitating factors.
